      "title": "Here's What Analysts Are Forecasting For GlaxoSmithKline Pharmaceuticals Limited (NSE:GLAXO) After Its Full-Year Results",
      "body": "GlaxoSmithKline Pharmaceuticals Limited ( NSE:GLAXO ) came out with its yearly results last week, and we wanted to see...",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/stocks/in/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nse-glaxo/glaxosmithkline-pharmaceuticals-shares/news/heres-what-analysts-are-forecasting-for-glaxosmithkline-phar",
      "raw_subtype": "article"
    },
    {
      "id": "b9eb9f41-a524-4bf6-bc05-16c9ba5d8c9d",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-15T12:09:22.000Z",
      "title": "Dividend increased to ₹57.00",
      "body": "Dividend of ₹57.00 is 36% higher than last year. Ex-date: 29th May 2026 Payment date: 30th July 2026 Dividend yield will be 2.3%, which is higher than the industry average of 0.8%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is covered by both earnings (70% earnings payout ratio) and cash flows (84% cash payout ratio). The dividend has increased by an average of 3.0% per year over the past 10 years. However, payments have been volatile during that time. EPS is expected to grow by 24% over the next 2 years, which should provide support to the dividend and adequate earnings cover.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "e9722713-5357-490b-97d9-b7ca32db5c3e",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-14T11:30:16.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS in line with expectations, revenues disappoint",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹61.15 (up from ₹54.76 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹39.7b (up 5.8% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹10.4b (up 12% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 26% (up from 25% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue missed analyst estimates by 1.6%. Earnings per share (EPS) were mostly in line with analyst estimates. Revenue is forecast to grow 8.2% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 12% growth forecast for the Pharmaceuticals industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 23% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 24% per year.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
